        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="true" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="true" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <HouseholdOperatingConditions numberOfOccupants="3" coolingSeasonMonths="4" isClothesWasherEnergySaver="true" isLightingEnergySaver="true" areAppliancesEnergySaver="true">
                <Thermostat heatingDaytime="21" heatingNighttime="18" cooling="25" />
            </HouseholdOperatingConditions>
            <AtypicalElectricalLoads deIcingCables="false" exteriorLighting="false" hotTub="false" heatedGarage="true" portableAirConditioning="false" pool="false" mixedUse="false" totalUnits="0" energyStarUnits="0" evChargingStation="false" outdoorGasAppliances="false" commonSpace="false" elevator="false" fitnessRoom="false" snowmeltSystem="false" unheatedGarage="false" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas:



Attic Hatch, Add gasket to hatch and add rigid insulation to top of hatch to compress seal.



Back doors along bottom, corners, around door handle.



Around the window glass seal is leaky on most windows. May be able to fix with silicon. If not, they may have to be replaced with ENERGY STARÂ® Zone 3 rated windows.</airSeal>
                <VentilationSystem>HRV Should be serviced and balanced.</VentilationSystem>
                <HotWaterSystem>See Heating upgrades.</HotWaterSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>Upgrade Heating and hot water systems to a gas combi boiler system. This would combine your heating and hot water into one system. Make sure to look for one that is ENERGY STARÂ® and has at least a 95% AFUE rating. 



This system will have direct supply/exhaust which will eliminate the need for the fresh supply air duct in the furnace room. This will decrease the amount of oil burned during the heating season and will reduce cold air entering the home. 



Only cut off the supply for combustion air if both heating and hot water are direct vented/condensing.



Please refer to Artic Energy Alliance for rebates on Heating/DHW upgrades and the criteria for these products. </HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
